<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<StringTableFile xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <Name>conversations\x_labyrinth\x1131_reflections</Name>
  <NextEntryID>1</NextEntryID>
  <EntryCount>144</EntryCount>
  <Entries>
    <Entry>
      <ID>91</ID>
      <DefaultText>Slow as glaciers, a vibration builds in the pylons beneath your feet as you consider which doppelganger to choose.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>92</ID>
      <DefaultText>Daggers, masks, paintbrushes, and amulets entwine around the mirror's frame. Stranger still is its reflection. 

A crowd of your doubles shove, argue, and fight. Most are drab, but a few vivid selves draw your attention. Each bears an intricate pentagonal tattoo on their head.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>94</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger moving cautiously through the crowd. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>95</ID>
      <DefaultText>Falling into a wary, well-balanced crouch, the doppelganger creeps towards you, scanning its surroundings with suspicious eyes. Each movement it makes is slow, subtle, and deliberate. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>96</ID>
      <DefaultText>Unfolding from the crouch, the doppelganger waits for your decision. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>97</ID>
      <DefaultText>"I want to consider the other choices."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>98</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doppelganger returns to the crowd. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>99</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>100</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double steps *into* you, filling you, making you whole.

Your decision awakens and unlocks vast mechanisms behind the walls. A grotesque noise rings through both worlds, like a bell if bells could rot. Something is coming...

{ANIM: Reflections steps into PC and vanishes.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>101</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger with the charming smile. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>102</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double swaggers forward and tells an outrageous story in a warm, sincere voice, full of confidential asides and unexpected twists.

You're almost certain most of it is lies, but cannot separate them from the truth.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>103</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doppelganger finishes its story with a flourish, and waits for your decision. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>104</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>105</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger with the clever eyes. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>106</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double approaches, but a thug charges from the crowd and brandishes a knife in its face.

Speaking in your voice, your double calms him with disarming wit and outright lies.

The thug scowls, lowers his knife, and apologizes.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>107</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doppelganger turns to you, waiting for your decision.
</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>108</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>109</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger slipping gracefully through the mob.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>110</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double darts forward, leans out of the mirror, and gently *pokes* your nose. When you try to return the gesture, it dodges, laughing.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>111</ID>
      <DefaultText>It chuckles, waiting for your decision. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>112</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>113</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the intelligent doppelganger with the furrowed brow. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>114</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doppelganger holds itself erect among the pressing crowd. It meets your eyes with a confident gaze, triggering familiar memories in the back of your mind...</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>115</ID>
      <DefaultText>When you return from your contemplation, the doppelganger is waiting for your decision with a knowing smile. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>116</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>117</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the learned doppelganger reclining on a throne of books.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>118</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double tucks a few books under its arm and approaches.

It lectures on prior-world technologies: sentient city defenses, shields used by a Steadfast battalion, and bacteria that were perhaps once beneficial, now mutated into a grotesque, weaponized disease.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>119</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doppelganger falls silent, waiting for your decision.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>120</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>121</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger tinkering with a mechanical device. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>122</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double presents a nineteen-sided device bristling with at least a hundred buttons and levers. With a few muttered words and precise movements, it activates it.

A bulging sphere of air shoots upward and bursts into serrated flower petals. The crowd cheers.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>123</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bowing, the doppelganger pockets the device, and waits for your decision. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>124</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>125</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger with the mystical symbol on its brow. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>126</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double shoulders through the crowd and pulls on an eight-fingered glove. It digs into the glass, tearing a hole shaped like a pointed ear.

Carefully, it speaks an unfamiliar word into the ear. The ground seems to *turn*, as if you stand inside a door it has opened.

The hole vanishes. Nothing has changed. Or has it?</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>127</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doppelganger plucks the eight-fingered glove from its hand, and waits for your decision. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>128</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>129</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger observing all the others. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>130</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double slips around the crowd and signals you to be silent. Together, you scan the room for hazards, hearing every drip in the depths below.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>131</ID>
      <DefaultText>Quietly, the doppelganger waits for your decision.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>132</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>133</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the rugged doppelganger striding on the shoulders of the others. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>134</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double leaps down, boasting of adventures in unmapped wildernesses: dives into bottomless seas and races across burning, poisonous deserts.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>135</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doppelganger waits for your decision, flexing its limber joints. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>136</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>137</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the slick doppelganger that's smooth-talking the others.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>138</ID>
      <DefaultText>Grinning roguishly, your double drops stolen coins and approaches, drawing a dagger from a hidden wrist sheath.

It tosses the dagger, catches it by the blade, and whips it at your head. You almost duck before realizing the weapon is still in its hand.

Its smooth apology makes you forget your anger.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>139</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doppelganger spins the dagger back into its sheath and waits for your decision.  </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>140</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>141</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger moving stealthily through the crowd.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>142</ID>
      <DefaultText>You blink, and your double seems gone.

Then you hear a low chuckle behind you...</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>143</ID>
      <DefaultText>You blink again. It is back behind the glass, waiting for your decision.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>144</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>145</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the strong doppelganger shoving its way through the group. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>146</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double thunders toward you like a mountain on legs, scattering the others. Its eyes promise violence.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>147</ID>
      <DefaultText>A rumble comes from somewhere deep in its chest as it waits for your decision. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>148</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>149</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the strong-willed doppelganger. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>150</ID>
      <DefaultText>It reaches the other side of the mirror, and touches its side of the glass. The surface blurs, and a vision unfolds before you...</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>151</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double stands shackled in a jeering arena beneath a hulking executioner. Unbowed, it warns of what will follow its death. One by one, the crowd falls silent.

It meets the executioner's eyes. Trembling, he swings his axe and severs its chains.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>152</ID>
      <DefaultText>The arena fades into the squabbling crowd. Your strong-willed double lowers its hand and awaits your decision, chin held high.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>153</ID>
      <DefaultText />
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>154</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>155</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger running swift circles around the group. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>156</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your lean double sprints across the mirror-room and skids to a halt inches from plunging through the glass.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>157</ID>
      <DefaultText>It stretches, waiting for your decision. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>158</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>159</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the tough-looking doppelganger. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>160</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double braces itself, points at you, and taps its bare chin. It seems to want a punch.

It nods as the thought crosses your mind.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>161</ID>
      <DefaultText>Punch the doppelganger as hard as you can.

{ANIM: PC punches Reflection} </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>162</ID>
      <DefaultText>You strike your double's jaw through the glass with all your strength. Its head rocks aside, but it glances back at you and grins. 

{SOUND: Fist hitting face.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>163</ID>
      <DefaultText>Thumbing a spot of luminescent blood from its lips, the doppelganger waits for your decision. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>164</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>165</ID>
      <DefaultText>Kick the reflection into the pit.

{ANIM: PC kicks Reflection, Reflection falls into pit.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>166</ID>
      <DefaultText>You lash out with your foot, and strike the reflection square in the chest. With a startled yelp, it topples backward into the pit. Eventually, you hear a nasty *thud*, and cursing. 

After a few seconds, the reflection rematerializes at the edge of the pit, eyeing you sourly. Its only souvenirs from the long fall are a few glowing bruises and one nasty scrape. {SCRIPT: Reflection rematerializes}
</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>167</ID>
      <DefaultText>"I don't want to hit you."

{ANIM: Reflection reacts to invisible hit.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>168</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double nods sympathetically, then punches *itself* across the chin as hard as it can. It spits out a tooth and grins. 

{SOUND: Fist hitting face.}</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>169</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the hulking doppelganger with wrath in its eyes. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>170</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your double whirls a club, clearing a path through the crowd.

It stomps up, glowers at you, then strikes the ground and roars in your face.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>171</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doppelganger growls, waiting for your decision. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>172</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes. That is who I am."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>179</ID>
      <DefaultText>Step away from the mirror.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>182</ID>
      <DefaultText>Countless doppelgangers of you crowd the reflected version of this room. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>183</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>186</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>188</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>189</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>190</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>191</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>192</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>193</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>194</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>195</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>196</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>197</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>198</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>199</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>200</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>201</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 183</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>204</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the wrathful doppelganger again. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>206</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the tough-looking doppelganger again.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>207</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 207</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>209</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the swift doppelganger again. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>210</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the strong doppelganger again. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>212</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the stealthy doppelganger again.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>213</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the strong-willed doppelganger again.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>214</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the slick doppelganger again. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>215</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the rugged doppelganger again. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>216</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the observant doppelganger again. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>217</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger with the mystical symbol on its brow again. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>218</ID>
      <DefaultText>Summon the doppelganger with the mechanical device back. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>219</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the learned doppelganger again. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>220</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the intelligent doppelganger again.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>221</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the graceful doppelganger again. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>222</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger with the clever eyes again.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>223</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the doppelganger with the charming smile again.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>224</ID>
      <DefaultText>Point at the cautious doppelganger again. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>227</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 227</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>228</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Let me choose my own path."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>229</ID>
      <DefaultText>"No... I think I'll choose my own path after all."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>230</ID>
      <DefaultText>Bank 230</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>231</ID>
      <DefaultText>The countless doppelgangers freeze, watching you out of the corners of their eyes. You realize they're waiting to see if you're certain.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>232</ID>
      <DefaultText>Once again, the doppelgangers go still, waiting for you to confirm your choice. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>233</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Yes, I'm sure."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>234</ID>
      <DefaultText>"Actually, let me see my choices again."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>235</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doppelgangers resume their chaotic festival as nothing happened. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>236</ID>
      <DefaultText>Their eyes and actions reflect the memories you found in the orbs and the choices you made. Your hand twitches. Some bright doubles ignore you; a few turn, waiting for you to choose what you might become.

A rumble shakes the room. Vibration rises from the darkness below toward the ceiling.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>237</ID>
      <DefaultText>Your doppelganger gives you a respectful nod. </DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>238</ID>
      <DefaultText>The doubles freeze, watching you. Then they scatter, whooping, and vanish behind the mirror's ornate edges. Only your true double remains, yours to shape.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>239</ID>
      <DefaultText>[DEBUG] Show me the results of my choices.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>240</ID>
      <DefaultText>Descriptor: Anything 2 or greater should appear in the list of responses. If all of them are less than 2, then Tough should be the only option available (this should be very rare).

If anything of them are -1, then something is broken. 

Cautious: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Cautious]
Charming: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Charming]
Clever: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Clever]
Graceful: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Graceful]
Intelligent: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Intelligent]
Learned: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Learned]
Mechanical: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Mechanical]
Mystical: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Mystical]
Observant: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Observant]
Rugged: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Rugged]
Slick: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Slick]
Stealthy: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Stealthy]
Strong: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Strong]
Strong-Willed: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_StrongWilled]
Swift: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Swift]
Tough: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Tough]
Wrathful: [Global: x1131_Descriptor_Wrathful]</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>241</ID>
      <DefaultText>"These aren't me. I want to choose my own path."</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>243</ID>
      <DefaultText>[In the real game, at this point you'd have the opportunity to review and change your Stat Pool allocations and Descriptor.

Thus concludes this Alpha Systems Test. Thank you for playing. Please send us your thoughts through the in-game feedback button.]</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>245</ID>
      <DefaultText>The mirror fades, leaving a dark, open doorway. You take a deep breath and step through.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>246</ID>
      <DefaultText>[TEMP TEXT] Now it lets you choose your class. What do you choose?</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>247</ID>
      <DefaultText>[Glaive]</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>248</ID>
      <DefaultText>[Nano]</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>249</ID>
      <DefaultText>[Jack]</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>250</ID>
      <DefaultText>Greater than 1 means Glaive. Less than -1 means Nano. All else means Jack.

Class Leaning: [Global: x1131_ClassLeaning]</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>251</ID>
      <DefaultText />
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>252</ID>
      <DefaultText>The remaining doppelgangers scatter for the edges of the mirror and vanish. Your chosen identity steps forward. Its appearance changes as it steps out of the rippling glass.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>253</ID>
      <DefaultText>Its body grows stronger and more supple. Shadows of weapons flicker in its hand; different kinds of armor shimmer over it. You feel that it - you - would be comfortable with them all.

The word 'glaive' sounds in your mind.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>254</ID>
      <DefaultText>Its face is intelligent and confident. Shadows of devices from many past ages shimmer around it. You feel that it - you - would be comfortable with all of them.

The word 'nano' sounds in your mind.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
    <Entry>
      <ID>255</ID>
      <DefaultText>Its face is confident and clever. Shadows of weapons flicker in its hand; a few devices shimmer at its belt. You feel that it - you - would be comfortable in a variety of situations.

The word 'jack' sounds in your mind.</DefaultText>
      <FemaleText />
    </Entry>
  </Entries>
</StringTableFile>